  "_about": "OverAscii encoding used for protocol bytes on the serial console (SerialConsole), so every byte sent has its top bit set and can be told apart from console text. Made from RaftCore ProtocolOverAscii by linux_unit_tests/test_comms_framing_vectors --write - do not edit. Encoding: 0x00-0x0f -> 0x85, (b ^ 0x20) | 0x80; 0x10-0x7f -> b | 0x80; 0x80-0x8f -> 0x8e, b ^ 0x20; 0x90-0xff -> 0x8f, b. The bytes sent over the console are OverAscii(HDLC(frame)). console cases split a received stream as SerialConsole does: bytes >= 0x80 are decoded and passed to HDLC, other bytes are console text.",
